{"Images": [{"Name": "i0", "Description": "Cholesterol crystal embolism - associated acute kidney injury (CCE-AKI)", "Path": "images/CCE-AKI-artery", "Width": 617, "Height": 653, "MaxLevel": 0}], "Header": "**Cholesterol crystal embolism - associated acute kidney injury** is characterized by the obstruction of small renal vessels by cholesterol crystals released from atherosclerotic plaques. These emboli induce endothelial injury, ischemia, and activation of inflammatory pathways within the kidney vasculature. Complement involvement is also suspected.   \n\nBecause vascular damage is central to CCE-AKI pathophysiology, the renal arterial compartment represents a key site of analysis. ", "Rotation": 0, "Layout": {"Grid": [["i0"]]}, "Stories": [{"Name": "", "Description": "", "Waypoints": [{"Name": "Structure of the artery", "Description": "The renal artery plays a critical role in maintaining kidney perfusion and delivering oxygen and nutrients to renal tissues. Its vascular wall is composed of endothelial cells lining the lumen and smooth muscle cells that regulate blood flow. ", "Arrows": [], "Overlays": [], "Group": "Artery", "Masks": [], "ActiveMasks": [], "Zoom": 0.4270312500000001, "Pan": [0.47243491577335395, 0.5809288246522157]}, {"Name": "Complement activation", "Description": "The complement is a part of the immune system. It can be activated by three different pathways : the classical, lectin or alternative pathway. Here, a lot of deposit of C1 fragments can be observed. ", "Arrows": [], "Overlays": [], "Group": "Classical complement pathway", "Masks": [], "ActiveMasks": [], "Zoom": 0.42703125000000014, "Pan": [0.4724349157733537, 0.45621457158892625]}, {"Name": "Complement activation pt. 2", "Description": "MBL acts like C1q in the lectin pathway : it is necessary to initiate the complement cascade activation. It recognizes sugar patterns on pathogens and allows the formation of the C3 convertase. Here, there is not a lot of MBL deposit, suggesting that that pathway is not activated. ", "Arrows": [], "Overlays": [], "Group": "Lectin complement pathway", "Masks": [], "ActiveMasks": [], "Zoom": 0.42703125000000014, "Pan": [0.4724349157733537, 0.45621457158892625]}, {"Name": "Complement activation pt. 3", "Description": "C1q - antibodies are observed, which would suggest that the classical pathway is activated. ", "Arrows": [], "Overlays": [], "Group": "Complement-antibodies complexes", "Masks": [], "ActiveMasks": [], "Zoom": 0.4270312500000001, "Pan": [0.47243491577335417, 0.4562145715889252]}, {"Name": "Terminal pathway", "Description": "There is a lot of deposition of C9 within the artery, indicating that the **membrane attack complex (MAC)** is efficiently formed. ", "Arrows": [], "Overlays": [], "Group": "Activated complement", "Masks": [], "ActiveMasks": [], "Zoom": 0.4270312500000001, "Pan": [0.47243491577335417, 0.4562145715889252]}, {"Name": "Immune infiltration", "Description": "The activation of the complement leads to the formation of two anaphylatoxins, C3a and C5a, whose role is to recruit immune cells to sites of complement activation. Here, there is immune infiltration of lymphocytes (CD3) but other immune cells also seem to detected. ", "Arrows": [{"Text": "Lymphocyte", "HideArrow": false, "Point": [0.8307225118216541, 0.0476525518304185], "Angle": 60}], "Overlays": [], "Group": "Immune cells", "Masks": [], "ActiveMasks": [], "Zoom": 0.4270312500000001, "Pan": [0.4724349157733539, 0.4840130836025858]}, {"Name": "Macrophage infiltration", "Description": "Heavy macrophage infiltration is observed in the tissue. ", "Arrows": [], "Overlays": [{"x": 0.25167628667224384, "y": 0.533409351440127, "width": 0.28174167581412357, "height": 0.25003049152335644}], "Group": "Macrophages", "Masks": [], "ActiveMasks": [], "Zoom": 0.42703125000000014, "Pan": [0.4724349157733537, 0.4840130836025858]}, {"Name": "Myeloid infiltration", "Description": "Myeloid cells (mostly macrophages) are infiltrated in the tissue, which indicates that complement activation lead to the recruitment of these immune cells : it plays a role in the inflammation observed in the arteries of patients diagnosed with CCE-AKI. ", "Arrows": [], "Overlays": [], "Group": "Myeloid cells", "Masks": [], "ActiveMasks": [], "Zoom": 0.42703125000000014, "Pan": [0.4724349157733537, 0.4840130836025858]}]}], "Channels": [{"Rendered": false, "Name": "DAPI", "Path": "DAPI_0__DAPI"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "C1q", "Path": "C1q_1__C1q"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "C5aR1", "Path": "C5aR1_4__C5aR1"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "CD68", "Path": "CD68_5__CD68"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "C3c", "Path": "C3c_6__C3c"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "CD163", "Path": "CD163_7__CD163"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "C3d", "Path": "C3d_8__C3d"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "CD45", "Path": "CD45_9__CD45"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "C1r", "Path": "C1r_10__C1r"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "CD20", "Path": "CD20_11__CD20"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "C1s", "Path": "C1s_12__C1s"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "Ki67", "Path": "Ki67_13__Ki67"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "C4d", "Path": "C4d_14__C4d"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "MBL", "Path": "MBL_15__MBL"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "C9", "Path": "C9_16__C9"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "aSMA", "Path": "aSMA_17__aSMA"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "CD3", "Path": "CD3_18__CD3"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "VCAM1", "Path": "VCAM1_19__VCAM1"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "CD11b", "Path": "CD11b_20__CD11b"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "CD31", "Path": "CD31_21__CD31"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "Megalin", "Path": "Megalin_22__Megalin"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "MPO", "Path": "MPO_23__MPO"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "IgG", "Path": "IgG_24__IgG"}], "Masks": [], "Groups": [{"Name": "DAPI", "Colors": ["0000ff"], "Channels": ["DAPI"], "Descriptions": [""]}, {"Name": "C1q", "Colors": ["ffff00"], "Channels": ["C1q"], "Descriptions": [""]}, {"Name": "C5aR1", "Colors": ["cc41cc"]